    title_en: "Warning: Microsoft KB5120998 Optional Update May Cause Windows Cursor Anomalies and Reset Desktop Background to Black",
    summary_en: "Microsoft released the KB5120998 optional update, which aims to introduce features such as a movable taskbar, adjustable Start menu, and a more streamlined search box. However, according to user reports, this update may cause two main issues: first, custom cursors may reset to the default, larger white cursor, and cannot be restored; and second, the desktop wallpaper may be cleared and reset to solid black. Affected users report that even if they manually set the background, it continues to revert to black after logging out or restarting. Although some users are unaffected, due to the widespread nature of the problem and the current only temporary workaround being the complete removal of the KB5120998 update, the article advises users to temporarily delay installing this update and await an official Microsoft fix. Microsoft has not yet officially acknowledged these issues, but users should monitor official announcements.",
